\\n\\n\") |   \\n[ <::before> ISSUE_TRIAGE.md  ](/root/openhands/-/blob/main/ISSUE_TRIAGE.md?ref_type=heads \"ISSUE_TRIAGE.md\") |  [ docs: Add doc on how issues are triaged (#2928) ](/root/openhands/-/commit/214f728d32619c8fd29aa0a0499c26fc886fabf0 \"docs: Add doc on how issues are triaged \\\\(#2928\\\\)\\n\\n* docs: Add doc on how issues are triaged\\r\\n\\r\\n* Update some wordings\") |   \\n[ <::before> LICENSE  ](/root/openhands/-/blob/main/LICENSE?ref_type=heads \"LICENSE\") |  [ Create MIT LICENSE (#8) ](/root/openhands/-/commit/39add27f15586b86f46a586f89754d7c799918f3 \"Create MIT LICENSE \\\\(#8\\\\)\\n\\n\") |   \\n[ <::before> MANIFEST.in  ](/root/openhands/-/blob/main/MANIFEST.in?ref_type=heads \"MANIFEST.in\") |  [ exclude Python cache files/folders from sdist to avoid permission errors at runtime (#3381) ](/root/openhands/-/commit/19bc06198de33c5a9b614701675d8409c7439cec \"exclude Python cache files/folders from sdist to avoid permission errors at runtime \\\\(#3381\\\\)\\n\\n\") |   \\n[ <::before> Makefile  ](/root/openhands/-/blob/main/Makefile?ref_type=heads \"Makefile\") |  [ Fix: uvicorn reloading when python files in workspace change, & started section for debugging instructions for developers (#4041) ](/root/openhands/-/commit/01317138e288c30718938be7db3ab03499dee3aa \"Fix: uvicorn reloading when python files in workspace change, & started section for debugging instructions for developers \\\\(#4041\\\\)\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Engel Nyst <enyst@users.noreply.github.com>\") |   \\n[ <::before> README.md  ](/root/openhands/-/blob/main/README.md?ref_type=heads \"README.md\") |  [ Update README to decrease unsuccessful drivebys (#4091) ](/root/openhands/-/commit/c7fe39998c2cd844bc6546354d6a866c24018c1a \"Update README to decrease unsuccessful drivebys \\\\(#4091\\\\)\\n\\n\") |   \\n[ <::before> compose.yml  ](/root/openhands/-/blob/main/compose.yml?ref_type=heads \"compose.yml\") |  [ chore: Add docker files for developing inside container. (#3911) ](/root/openhands/-/commit/f7ebc1cf1f1f4ae306d1e630ac57b618d0d85810 \"chore: Add docker files for developing inside container. \\\\(#3911\\\\)\\n\\n\") |   \\n[ <::before> config.template.toml  ](/root/openhands/-/blob/main/config.template.toml?ref_type=heads \"config.template.toml\") |  [ Vision and prompt caching fixes (#4014) ](/root/openhands/-/commit/e582806004cf4bad0934dd640ab1631841d7c664 \"Vision and prompt caching fixes \\\\(#4014\\\\)\\n\\n\") |   \\n[ <::before> poetry.lock  ](/root/openhands/-/blob/main/poetry.lock?ref_type=heads \"poetry.lock\") |  |   \\n[ <::before> pydoc-markdown.yml  ](/root/openhands/-/blob/main/pydoc-markdown.yml?ref_type=heads \"pydoc-markdown.yml\") |  |   \\n[ <::before> pyproject.toml  ](/root/openhands/-/blob/main/pyproject.toml?ref_type=heads \"pyproject.toml\") |  |   \\n[ <::before> pytest.ini  ](/root/openhands/-/blob/main/pytest.ini?ref_type=heads \"pytest.ini\") |  |   \\n  \\n[ **README.md** ](/root/openhands/-/blob/main/README.md?ref_type=heads)\\n\\n[ ](/root/openhands/-/raw/main/docs/static/img/logo.png)\\n\\n#  OpenHands: Code Less, Make More \\n\\n[ ](https://github.com/All-Hands-AI/OpenHands/graphs/contributors) [ ](https://github.com/All-Hands-AI/OpenHands/stargazers) [ ](https://codecov.io/github/All-Hands-AI/OpenHands?branch=main) [ ](https://github.com/All-Hands-AI/OpenHands/blob/main/LICENSE)   \\n[ ](https://join.slack.com/t/opendevin/shared_invite/zt-2oikve2hu-UDxHeo8nsE69y6T7yFX_BA) [ ](https://discord.gg/ESHStjSjD4) [ ](https://github.com/All-Hands-AI/OpenHands/blob/main/CREDITS.md)   \\n[ ](https://docs.all-hands.dev/modules/usage/getting-started) [ ](https://arxiv.org/abs/2407.16741) [ ](https://huggingface.co/spaces/OpenHands/evaluation)\\n\\n* * *\\n\\nWelcome to OpenHands (formerly OpenDevin), a platform for software development agents powered by AI. \\n\\nOpenHands agents can do anything a human developer can: modify code, run commands, browse the web, call APIs, and yes\u2014even copy code snippets from StackOverflow. \\n\\nLearn more at [ docs.all-hands.dev ](https://docs.all-hands.dev) , or jump to the  Quick Start  . \\n\\n[ ](/root/openhands/-/raw/main/docs/static/img/screenshot.png)\\n\\n##  <::after> \u26a1 Quick Start \\n\\nThe easiest way to run OpenHands is in Docker. You can change ` WORKSPACE_BASE ` below to point OpenHands to existing code that you\\'d like to modify. \\n\\nSee the [ Getting Started ](https://docs.all-hands.dev/modules/usage/getting-started) guide for system requirements and more information. \\n    \\n    \\n    export WORKSPACE_BASE=$(pwd)/workspace\\n    \\n    docker pull ghcr.io/all-hands-ai/runtime:0.9-nikolaik\\n    \\n    docker run -it --pull=always \\\\\\n        -e SANDBOX_RUNTIME_CONTAINER_IMAGE=ghcr.io/all-hands-ai/runtime:0.9-nikolaik \\\\\\n        -e SANDBOX_USER_ID=$(id -u) \\\\\\n        -e WORKSPACE_MOUNT_PATH=$WORKSPACE_BASE \\\\\\n        -v $WORKSPACE_BASE:/opt/workspace_base \\\\\\n        -v /var/run/docker.sock:/var/run/docker.sock \\\\\\n        -p 3000:3000 \\\\\\n        --add-host host.docker.internal:host-gateway \\\\\\n        --name openhands-app-$(date +%Y%m%d%H%M%S) \\\\\\n        ghcr.io/all-hands-ai/openhands:0.9\\n\\nYou\\'ll find OpenHands running at [ http://localhost:3000 ](http://localhost:3000) ! \\n\\nYou\\'ll need a model provider and API key. One option that works well: [ Claude 3.5 Sonnet ](https://www.anthropic.com/api) , but you have [ many options ](https://docs.all-hands.dev/modules/usage/llms) . \\n\\n* * *\\n\\nYou can also run OpenHands in a scriptable [ headless mode ](https://docs.all-hands.dev/modules/usage/how-to/headless-mode) , or as an [ interactive CLI ](https://docs.all-hands.dev/modules/usage/how-to/cli-mode) . \\n\\nVisit [ Getting Started ](https://docs.all-hands.dev/modules/usage/getting-started) for more information and setup instructions. \\n\\nIf you want to modify the OpenHands source code, check out [ Development.md ](https://github.com/All-Hands-AI/OpenHands/blob/main/Development.md) . \\n\\nHaving issues? The [ Troubleshooting Guide ](https://docs.all-hands.dev/modules/usage/troubleshooting) can help. \\n\\n##  <::after> \ud83d\udcd6 Documentation \\n\\nTo learn more about the project, and for tips on using OpenHands, **check out our[ documentation ](https://docs.all-hands.dev/modules/usage/getting-started) ** . \\n\\nThere you\\'ll find resources on how to use different LLM providers, troubleshooting resources, and advanced configuration options. \\n\\n##  <::after> \ud83e\udd1d How to Contribute \\n\\nOpenHands is a community-driven project, and we welcome contributions from everyone. Whether you\\'re a developer, a researcher, or simply enthusiastic about advancing the field of software engineering with AI, there are many ways to get involved: \\n\\n  * <::marker> **Code Contributions:** Help us develop new agents, core functionality, the frontend and other interfaces, or sandboxing solutions. \\n  * <::marker> **Research and Evaluation:** Contribute to our understanding of LLMs in software engineering, participate in evaluating the models, or suggest improvements. \\n  * <::marker> **Feedback and Testing:** Use the OpenHands toolset, report bugs, suggest features, or provide feedback on usability. \\n\\n\\n\\nFor details, please check [ CONTRIBUTING.md ](/root/openhands/-/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md) . \\n\\n##  <::after> \ud83e\udd16 Join Our Community \\n\\nWhether you\\'re a developer, a researcher, or simply enthusiastic about OpenHands, we\\'d love to have you in our community. Let\\'s make software engineering better together! \\n\\n  * <::marker> [ Slack workspace ](https://join.slack.com/t/opendevin/shared_invite/zt-2oikve2hu-UDxHeo8nsE69y6T7yFX_BA) \\\\- Here we talk about research, architecture, and future development. \\n  * <::marker> [ Discord server ](https://discord.gg/ESHStjSjD4) \\\\- This is a community-run server for general discussion, questions, and feedback. \\n\\n\\n\\n##  <::after> \ud83d\udcc8 Progress \\n\\n[ ](https://star-history.com/#All-Hands-AI/OpenHands&Date)\\n\\n##  <::after> \ud83d\udcdc License \\n\\nDistributed under the MIT License. See [ ` LICENSE ` ](/root/openhands/-/blob/main/LICENSE) for more information. \\n\\n##  <::after> \ud83d\ude4f Acknowledgements \\n\\nOpenHands is built by a large number of contributors, and every contribution is greatly appreciated! We also build upon other open source projects, and we are deeply thankful for their work. \\n\\nFor a list of open source projects and licenses used in OpenHands, please see our [ CREDITS.md ](/root/openhands/-/blob/main/CREDITS.md) file. \\n\\n##  <::after> \ud83d\udcda Cite \\n    \\n    \\n    @misc{opendevin,\\n          title={{OpenDevin: An Open Platform for AI Software Developers as Generalist Agents}},\\n          author={Xingyao Wang and Boxuan Li and Yufan Song and Frank F. Xu and Xiangru Tang and Mingchen Zhuge and Jiayi Pan and Yueqi Song and Bowen Li and Jaskirat Singh and Hoang H. Tran and Fuqiang Li and Ren Ma and Mingzhang Zheng and Bill Qian and Yanjun Shao and Niklas Muennighoff and Yizhe Zhang and Binyuan Hui and Junyang Lin and Robert Brennan and Hao Peng and Heng Ji and Graham Neubig},\\n          year={2024},\\n          eprint={2407.16741},\\n          archivePrefix={arXiv},\\n          primaryClass={cs.SE},\\n          url={https://arxiv.org/abs/2407.16741},\\n    }\\n', url='http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/openhands', trigger_by_action='browse_interactive', screenshot_path='/outputs/.browser_screenshots/screenshot_20251108_045114_351281.png', error=False, observation=<ObservationType.BROWSE: 'browse'>, goal_image_urls=[], open_pages_urls=['http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/openhands'], active_page_index=0, last_browser_action=\"\\ngoto('http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/openhands')\\nnoop(2000)\\n\", last_browser_action_error='', focused_element_bid='85'), BrowseInteractiveAction(browser_actions='\\nclick(\\'1669\\')  # Click on the \"evaluation\" directory link\\nnoop(2000)\\n', thought='I can see the OpenHands repository is loaded. Now I need to explore the repository structure to find benchmark files or documentation. Let me click on the \"evaluation\" directory which likely contains benchmark information.', browsergym_send_msg_to_user='', action=<ActionType.BROWSE_INTERACTIVE: 'browse_interactive'>, security_risk=None), BrowserOutputObservation(content='Skip to main content \\n\\n##  Primary navigation \\n\\n[ Homepage  ](/)\\n\\nCreate new... \\n\\n  * In this project \\n\\n    * [ New issue  ](/root/openhands/-/issues/new)\\n    * [ New merge request  ](/root/openhands/-/merge_requests/new)\\n    * [ New snippet  ](/root/openhands/-/snippets/new)\\n    * Invite team members \\n  * In GitLab \\n\\n    * [ New project/repository  ](/projects/new)\\n    * [ New group  ](/groups/new)\\n    * [ New snippet  ](/-/snippets/new)\\n\\n\\n\\nAdministrator user\u2019s menu \\n\\n  *     * [ Administrator  @root  ](/root)\\n  *     * Set status \\n    * [ Edit profile  ](/-/user_settings/profile)\\n    * [ Preferences  ](/-/profile/preferences)\\n  *     * [ Sign out  ](/users/sign_out)\\n\\n\\n\\n[ 84  ](/dashboard/issues?assignee_username=root)\\n\\n99+ \\n\\n  * Merge requests \\n\\n    * [ Assigned  7  ](/dashboard/merge_requests?assignee_username=root)\\n    * [ Review requests  157  ](/dashboard/merge_requests?reviewer_username=root)\\n\\n\\n\\n[ ](/dashboard/todos)\\n\\nSearch or go to\u2026 \\n\\nProject \\n\\n  * [ O  openhands  ](/root/openhands)\\n\\n\\n\\nPinned \\n\\n  * [ Issues  120  ](/root/openhands/-/issues)\\n  * [ Merge requests  34  ](/root/openhands/-/merge_requests)\\n\\n\\n\\n* * *\\n\\n  * Manage \\n\\n    * [ Activity  ](/root/openhands/activity)\\n    * [ Members  ](/root/openhands/-/project_members)\\n    * [ Labels  ](/root/openhands/-/labels)\\n\\n  * Plan \\n\\n    * [ Issues  120  ](/root/openhands/-/issues)\\n    * [ Issue boards  ](/root/openhands/-/boards)\\n    * [ Mile