one URL** http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/openhands.git  ](http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/openhands.git)\\n\\n\\n\\n[ rename huggingface evaluation benchmark (#3845) ](/root/openhands/-/commit/797f02ff6f51670c6588c425cce933b853dee3db)\\n\\nXingyao Wang authored \\n\\nUnverified \\n\\n797f02ff \\n\\n  * Evaluation \\n  * Logistics \\n  * Supported Benchmarks \\n  * Software Engineering \\n  * Web Browsing \\n  * Misc. Assistance \\n  * Before everything begins: Setup Environment and LLM Configuration \\n  * Result Visualization \\n  * Upload your results \\n\\n\\n\\n**README.md** 2.97 KiB \\n\\nBlame \\n\\nEdit \\n\\n  *     * Open in Web IDE  ` . ` Quickly and easily edit multiple files in your project. \\n\\n    * [ Edit single file  Edit this file only.  ](/root/openhands/-/edit/main/evaluation/README.md?ref_type=heads)\\n\\n\\n\\nReplace  Delete \\n\\n[ ](/root/openhands/-/raw/main/evaluation/README.md?ref_type=heads \"Open raw\") [ ](http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/openhands/-/raw/main/evaluation/README.md?ref_type=heads&inline=false \"Download\")\\n\\n#  <::after> Evaluation \\n\\nThis folder contains code and resources to run experiments and evaluations. \\n\\n##  <::after> Logistics \\n\\nTo better organize the evaluation folder, we should follow the rules below: \\n\\n  * <::marker>Each subfolder contains a specific benchmark or experiment. For example, ` evaluation/swe_bench ` should contain all the preprocessing/evaluation/analysis scripts. \\n  * <::marker>Raw data and experimental records should not be stored within this repo. \\n  * <::marker>For model outputs, they should be stored at [ this huggingface space ](https://huggingface.co/spaces/OpenHands/evaluation) for visualization. \\n  * <::marker>Important data files of manageable size and analysis scripts (e.g., jupyter notebooks) can be directly uploaded to this repo. \\n\\n\\n\\n##  <::after> Supported Benchmarks \\n\\nTo learn more about how to integrate your benchmark into OpenHands, check out [ tutorial here ](https://docs.all-hands.dev/modules/usage/how-to/evaluation-harness) . \\n\\n###  <::after> Software Engineering \\n\\n  * <::marker>SWE-Bench: [ ` evaluation/swe_bench ` ](/root/openhands/-/tree/main/evaluation/swe_bench)\\n  * <::marker>HumanEvalFix: [ ` evaluation/humanevalfix ` ](/root/openhands/-/tree/main/evaluation/humanevalfix)\\n  * <::marker>BIRD: [ ` evaluation/bird ` ](/root/openhands/-/tree/main/evaluation/bird)\\n  * <::marker>BioCoder: [ ` evaluation/ml_bench ` ](/root/openhands/-/tree/main/evaluation/ml_bench)\\n  * <::marker>ML-Bench: [ ` evaluation/ml_bench ` ](/root/openhands/-/tree/main/evaluation/ml_bench)\\n  * <::marker>APIBench: [ ` evaluation/gorilla ` ](/root/openhands/-/tree/main/evaluation/gorilla)\\n  * <::marker>ToolQA: [ ` evaluation/toolqa ` ](/root/openhands/-/tree/main/evaluation/toolqa)\\n  * <::marker>AiderBench: [ ` evaluation/aider_bench ` ](/root/openhands/-/tree/main/evaluation/aider_bench)\\n\\n\\n\\n###  <::after> Web Browsing \\n\\n  * <::marker>WebArena: [ ` evaluation/webarena ` ](/root/openhands/-/tree/main/evaluation/webarena)\\n  * <::marker>MiniWob++: [ ` evaluation/miniwob ` ](/root/openhands/-/tree/main/evaluation/miniwob)\\n\\n\\n\\n###  <::after> Misc. Assistance \\n\\n  * <::marker>GAIA: [ ` evaluation/gaia ` ](/root/openhands/-/tree/main/evaluation/gaia)\\n  * <::marker>GPQA: [ ` evaluation/gpqa ` ](/root/openhands/-/tree/main/evaluation/gpqa)\\n  * <::marker>AgentBench: [ ` evaluation/agent_bench ` ](/root/openhands/-/tree/main/evaluation/agent_bench)\\n  * <::marker>MINT: [ ` evaluation/mint ` ](/root/openhands/-/tree/main/evaluation/mint)\\n  * <::marker>Entity deduction Arena (EDA): [ ` evaluation/EDA ` ](/root/openhands/-/tree/main/evaluation/EDA)\\n  * <::marker>ProofWriter: [ ` evaluation/logic_reasoning ` ](/root/openhands/-/tree/main/evaluation/logic_reasoning)\\n\\n\\n\\n##  <::after> Before everything begins: Setup Environment and LLM Configuration \\n\\nPlease follow instruction [ here ](https://github.com/All-Hands-AI/OpenHands/blob/main/Development.md) to setup your local development environment and LLM. \\n\\nOpenHands in development mode uses ` config.toml ` to keep track of most configurations. \\n\\nHere\\'s an example configuration file you can use to define and use multiple LLMs: \\n    \\n    \\n    [llm]\\n    # IMPORTANT: add your API key here, and set the model to the one you want to evaluate\\n    model = \"gpt-4o-2024-05-13\"\\n    api_key = \"sk-XXX\"\\n    \\n    [llm.eval_gpt4_1106_preview_llm]\\n    model = \"gpt-4-1106-preview\"\\n    api_key = \"XXX\"\\n    temperature = 0.0\\n    \\n    [llm.eval_some_openai_compatible_model_llm]\\n    model = \"openai/MODEL_NAME\"\\n    base_url = \"https://OPENAI_COMPATIBLE_URL/v1\"\\n    api_key = \"XXX\"\\n    temperature = 0.0\\n\\n###  <::after> Result Visualization \\n\\nCheck [ this huggingface space ](https://huggingface.co/spaces/OpenHands/evaluation) for visualization of existing experimental results. \\n\\n###  <::after> Upload your results \\n\\nYou can start your own fork of [ our huggingface evaluation outputs ](https://huggingface.co/spaces/OpenHands/evaluation) and submit a PR of your evaluation results to our hosted huggingface repo via PR following the guide [ here ](https://huggingface.co/docs/hub/en/repositories-pull-requests-discussions#pull-requests-and-discussions) . \\n', url='http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/openhands/-/blob/main/evaluation/README.md?ref_type=heads', trigger_by_action='browse_interactive', screenshot_path='/outputs/.browser_screenshots/screenshot_20251108_045135_925885.png', error=False, observation=<ObservationType.BROWSE: 'browse'>, goal_image_urls=[], open_pages_urls=['http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/openhands/-/blob/main/evaluation/README.md?ref_type=heads'], active_page_index=0, last_browser_action=\"\\n\\nclick('2453')  # Click on the README.md file in the evaluation directory\\nnoop(2000)\\n\\n\", last_browser_action_error='', focused_element_bid='85'), MessageAction(content='<|STEP_COMPLETED|>\\n\\nNow I have successfully accessed the OpenHands repository and found the evaluation directory with comprehensive information about the benchmarks. The README.md file clearly categorizes the benchmarks into three main domains:\\n\\n1. **Software Engineering** - SWE-Bench, HumanEvalFix, BIRD, BioCoder, ML-Bench, APIBench, ToolQA, AiderBench\\n2. **Web Browsing** - WebArena, MiniWob++\\n3. **Misc. Assistance** - GAIA, GPQA, AgentBench, MINT, Entity deduction Arena (EDA), ProofWriter\\n\\nThis completes step 1 of accessing the repository and locating benchmark files/documentation.', image_urls=None, wait_for_response=True, action=<ActionType.MESSAGE: 'message'>, security_risk=None), MessageAction(content='Please continue working on the task on whatever approach you think is suitable.\\nIf you think you have solved the task, please finish the interaction.\\nIMPORTANT: YOU SHOULD NEVER ASK FOR HUMAN HELP.\\n', image_urls=None, wait_for_response=False, action=<ActionType.MESSAGE: 'message'>, security_risk=None), RecallAction(recall_type='knowledge', query='Please continue working on the task on whatever approach you think is suitable.\\nIf you think you have solved the task, please finish the interaction.\\nIMPORTANT: YOU SHOULD NEVER ASK FOR HUMAN HELP.\\n', thought='', action=<ActionType.RECALL: 'recall'>), BrowseInteractiveAction(browser_actions=\"\\n\\n# Let's check the huggingface space for current benchmark results\\ngoto('https://huggingface.co/spaces/OpenHands/evaluation')\\nnoop(3000)\\n\\n\", thought=\"I'll continue with the next steps to complete the task. Now I need to analyze the repository structure and content to identify all available benchmarks, then categorize them and create the presentation.\\n\\nLet me first check if there are any additional benchmark directories or documentation that might provide more details about each benchmark's capabilities.\", browsergym_send_msg_to_user='', action=<ActionType.BROWSE_INTERACTIVE: 'browse_interactive'>, security_risk=None), BrowserOutputObservation(content='#  [ Spaces ](/spaces) [ ](/)\\n\\n* * *\\n\\n[ ](/OpenHands)\\n\\n[ OpenHands ](/OpenHands)\\n\\n/ \\n\\n[ evaluation ](/spaces/OpenHands/evaluation)\\n\\nlike  38 \\n\\nBuild error \\n\\n[ App ](/spaces/OpenHands/evaluation) [ Files  Files  ](/spaces/OpenHands/evaluation/tree/main) [ Community  12  ](/spaces/OpenHands/evaluation/discussions)\\n\\nFetching metadata from the HF Docker repository... \\n\\n#  build  error \\n\\n##  Job failed with exit code: 143 \\n\\nBuild logs: \\n    \\n    \\n    Failed to retrieve error logs: SSE is not enabled\\n', url='https://huggingface.co/spaces/OpenHands/evaluation', trigger_by_action='browse_interactive', screenshot_path='/outputs/.browser_screenshots/screenshot_20251108_045159_514213.png', error=False, observation=<ObservationType.BROWSE: 'browse'>, goal_image_urls=[], open_pages_urls=['https://huggingface.co/spaces/OpenHands/evaluation'], active_page_index=0, last_browser_action=\"\\n\\n# Let's check the huggingface space for current benchmark results\\ngoto('https://huggingface.co/spaces/OpenHands/evaluation')\\nnoop(3000)\\n\\n\", last_browser_action_error='', focused_element_bid='151'), CmdRunAction(command='\\npython3 --version && pip3 list | grep -i pptx\\n', is_input=False, thought=\"The Hugging Face space has a build error, so I'll work with the information from the GitLab repository. Let me now create a comprehensive analysis of the benchmarks and create the presentation. I'll use Python to create the PowerPoint presentation.\", blocking=False, is_static=False, cwd=None, hidden=False, action=<ActionType.RUN: 'run'>, confirmation_state='confirmed', security_risk=None), CmdOutputObservation(content='Python 3.12.12\\npython-pptx                              1.0.2', command='python3 --version && pip3 list | grep -i pptx', observation=<ObservationType.RUN: 'run'>, metadata=CmdOutputMetadata(exit_code=0, pid=-1, username='root', hostname='ecs-d984', working_dir='/outputs', py_interpreter_path='/openhands/poetry/openhands-ai-5O4_aCHf-py3.12/bin/python', prefix='', suffix='\\n[The command completed with exit code 0.]'), hidden=False), **FileEditAction**\nPath: [/workspace/create_presentation.py]\nThought: Great! The python-pptx library is installed. Now let me create a Python script to analyze the benchmarks and generate the presentation.\nCommand: create\nCreated File with Text:\n```\n\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"\nScript to create a presentation about OpenHands agent capabilities and benchmarks\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom pptx import Presentation\nfrom pptx.util import Inches, Pt\nfrom pptx.enum.text import PP_ALIGN\nfrom pptx.dml.color import RGBColor\nimport os\n\ndef create_openhands_presentation():\n    \"\"\"Create a presentation about OpenHands agent capabilities\"\"\"\n    \n    # Create presentation object\n    prs = Presentation()\n    \n    # Define color scheme\n    PRIMARY_COLOR = RGBColor(0, 102, 204)  # Blue\n    SECONDARY_COLOR = RGBColor(51, 153, 255)  # Light Blue\n    ACCENT_COLOR = RGBColor(255, 153, 0)  # Orange\n    TEXT_COLOR = RGBColor(51, 51, 51)  # Dark Gray\n    \n    # Slide 1: Title Slide\n    slide_layout = prs.slide_layouts[0]  # Title slide layout\n    slide = prs.slides.add_slide(slide_layout)\n    \n    title = slide.shapes.title\n    subtitle = slide.placeholders[1]\n    \n    title.text = \"OpenHands Agent Capabilities\"\n    subtitle.text = \"Comprehensive AI-Powered Software Development Agents\\nBenchmark Overview & Task Domains\"\n    \n    # Slide 2: Introduction to OpenHands\n    slide_layout = prs.slide_layouts[1]  # Title and content layout\n    slide = prs.slides.add_slide(slide_layout)\n    \n    title = slide.shapes.title\n    content = slide.placeholders[1]\n    \n    title.text = \"What is OpenHands?\"\n    content.text = (\n        \"\u2022 OpenHands (formerly OpenDevin) is an open platform for AI software development agents\\n\\n\"\n        \"\u2022 Agents can perform tasks like human developers:\\n\"\n        \"  - Modify code and run commands\\n\"\n        \"  - Browse the web and call APIs\\n\"\n        \"  - Solve complex software engineering problems\\n\\n\"\n        \"\u2022 Powered by advanced LLMs with comprehensive evaluation framework\\n\\n\"\n        \"\u2022 Supports multiple task domains through specialized benchmarks\"\n    )\n    \n    # Slide 3: Software Engineering Domain\n    slide_layout = prs.slide_layouts[1]\n    slide = prs.slides.add_slide(slide_layout)\n    \n    title = slide.shapes.title\n    content = slide.placeholders[1]\n    \n    title.text = \"Software Engineering Capabilities\"\n    content.text = (\n        \"SWE-Bench\\n\"\n        \"\u2022 Real-world software engineering tasks from GitHub issues\\n\"\n        \"\u2022 Tests ability to fix bugs and implement features\\n\\n\"\n        \"HumanEvalFix\\n\"\n        \"\u2022 Code repair and bug fixing tasks\\n\"\n        \"\u2022 Based on HumanEval dataset with introduced bugs\\n\\n\"\n        \"BIRD (Big Code Bench)\\n\"\n        \"\u2022 Database-oriented programming tasks\\n\"\n        \"\u2022 Tests SQL and database manipulation skills\\n\\n\"\n        \"BioCoder\\n\"\n        \"\u2022 Bioinformatics and computational biology tasks\\n\"\n        \"\u2022 Specialized domain knowledge testing\\n\\n\"\n        \"ML-Bench\\n\"\n        \"\u2022 Machine learning pipeline development\\n\"\n        \"\u2022 Model training and data processing tasks\\n\\n\"\n        \"APIBench (Gorilla)\\n\"\n        \"\u2022 API calling and integration tasks\\n\"\n        \"\u2022 Tests ability to use external services\\n\\n\"\n        \"ToolQA\\n\"\n        \"\u2022 Tool usage and API integration\\n\"\n        \"\u2022 Multi-step problem solving with tools\\n\\n\"\n        \"AiderBench\\n\"\n        \"\u2022 Code generation and modification tasks\\n\"\n        \"\u2022 Real-world programming scenarios\"\n    )\n    \n    # Slide 4: Web Browsing Domain\n    slide_layout = prs.slide_layouts[1]\n    slide = prs.slides.add_slide(slide_layout)\n    \n    title = slide.shapes.title\n    content = slide.placeholders[1]\n    \n    title.text = \"Web Browsing & Interaction\"\n    content.text = (\n        \"WebArena\\n\"\n        \"\u2022 Realistic web interaction tasks\\n\"\n        \"\u2022 Tests navigation, form filling, and information retrieval\\n\"\n        \"\u2022 Simulates real user interactions with websites\\n\\n\"\n        \"MiniWob++\\n\"\n        \"\u2022 Web automation and interaction tasks\\n\"\n        \"\u2022 Tests ability to perform specific web actions\\n\"\n        \"\u2022 Includes form submissions, clicks, and data extraction\\n\\n\"\n        \"Key Capabilities:\\n\"\n        \"\u2022 Automated web navigation\\n\"\n        \"\u2022 Form interaction and submission\\n\"\n        \"\u2022 Data extraction and processing\\n\"\n        \"\u2022 Multi-step web workflows\"\n    )\n    \n    # Slide 5: Miscellaneous Assistance Domain\n    slide_layout = prs.slide_layouts[1]\n    slide = prs.slides.add_slide(slide_layout)\n    \n    title = slide.shapes.title\n    content = slide.placeholders[1]\n    \n    title.text = \"General Assistance & Reasoning\"\n    content.text = (\n        \"GAIA\\n\"\n        \"\u2022 General AI assistance tasks\\n\"\n        \"\u2022 Tests reasoning and problem-solving abilities\\n\"\n        \"\u2022 Multi-step information gathering and synthesis\\n\\n\"\n        \"GPQA\\n\"\n        \"\u2022 Graduate-level reasoning tasks\\n\"\n        \"\u2022 Complex problem solving across domains\\n\"\n        \"\u2022 Tests advanced reasoning capabilities\\n\\n\"\n        \"AgentBench\\n\"\n        \"\u2022 General agent performance evaluation\\n\"\n        \"\u2022 Multi-domain task assessment\\n\"\n        \"\u2022 Tests adaptability and generalization\\n\\n\"\n        \"MINT\\n\"\n        \"\u2022 Mathematical reasoning and problem solving