mark (#3845) ](/root/openhands/-/commit/797f02ff6f51670c6588c425cce933b853dee3db \"rename huggingface evaluation benchmark \\\\(#3845\\\\)\\n\\n\") |   \\n[ <::before> README.md  ](/root/openhands/-/blob/main/evaluation/README.md \"README.md\") |  [ rename huggingface evaluation benchmark (#3845) ](/root/openhands/-/commit/797f02ff6f51670c6588c425cce933b853dee3db \"rename huggingface evaluation benchmark \\\\(#3845\\\\)\\n\\n\") |   \\n[ <::before> __init__.py  ](/root/openhands/-/blob/main/evaluation/__init__.py \"__init__.py\") |  [ feat(SWE-Bench environment) integrate SWE-Bench sandbox (#1468) ](/root/openhands/-/commit/2406b901df37b817831e82e2894e5f6d60ad5290 \"feat\\\\(SWE-Bench environment\\\\) integrate SWE-Bench sandbox \\\\(#1468\\\\)\\n\\n* add draft dockerfile for build all\\r\\n\\r\\n* add rsync for build\\r\\n\\r\\n* add all-in-one docker\\r\\n\\r\\n* update prepare scripts\\r\\n\\r\\n* Update swe_env_box.py\\r\\n\\r\\n* Add swe_entry.sh \\\\(buggy now\\\\)\\r\\n\\r\\n* Parse the test command in swe_entry.sh\\r\\n\\r\\n* Update README for instance eval in sandbox\\r\\n\\r\\n* revert specialized config\\r\\n\\r\\n* replace run_as_devin as an init arg\\r\\n\\r\\n* set container & run_as_root via args\\r\\n\\r\\n* update swe entry script\\r\\n\\r\\n* update env\\r\\n\\r\\n* remove mounting\\r\\n\\r\\n* allow error after swe_entry\\r\\n\\r\\n* update swe_env_box\\r\\n\\r\\n* move file\\r\\n\\r\\n* update gitignore\\r\\n\\r\\n* get swe_env_box a working demo\\r\\n\\r\\n* support faking user response & provide sandox ahead of time;\\r\\nalso return state for controller\\r\\n\\r\\n* tweak main to support adding controller kwargs\\r\\n\\r\\n* add module\\r\\n\\r\\n* initialize plugin for provided sandbox\\r\\n\\r\\n* add pip cache to plugin & fix jupyter kernel waiting\\r\\n\\r\\n* better print Observation output\\r\\n\\r\\n* add run infer scripts\\r\\n\\r\\n* update readme\\r\\n\\r\\n* add utility for ge...\") |   \\n  \\n[ **README.md** ](/root/openhands/-/blob/main/evaluation/README.md)\\n\\n#  <::after> Evaluation \\n\\nThis folder contains code and resources to run experiments and evaluations. \\n\\n##  <::after> Logistics \\n\\nTo better organize the evaluation folder, we should follow the rules below: \\n\\n  * <::marker>Each subfolder contains a specific benchmark or experiment. For example, ` evaluation/swe_bench ` should contain all the preprocessing/evaluation/analysis scripts. \\n  * <::marker>Raw data and experimental records should not be stored within this repo. \\n  * <::marker>For model outputs, they should be stored at [ this huggingface space ](https://huggingface.co/spaces/OpenHands/evaluation) for visualization. \\n  * <::marker>Important data files of manageable size and analysis scripts (e.g., jupyter notebooks) can be directly uploaded to this repo. \\n\\n\\n\\n##  <::after> Supported Benchmarks \\n\\nTo learn more about how to integrate your benchmark into OpenHands, check out [ tutorial here ](https://docs.all-hands.dev/modules/usage/how-to/evaluation-harness) . \\n\\n###  <::after> Software Engineering \\n\\n  * <::marker>SWE-Bench: [ ` evaluation/swe_bench ` ](/root/openhands/-/tree/main/evaluation/swe_bench)\\n  * <::marker>HumanEvalFix: [ ` evaluation/humanevalfix ` ](/root/openhands/-/tree/main/evaluation/humanevalfix)\\n  * <::marker>BIRD: [ ` evaluation/bird ` ](/root/openhands/-/tree/main/evaluation/bird)\\n  * <::marker>BioCoder: [ ` evaluation/ml_bench ` ](/root/openhands/-/tree/main/evaluation/ml_bench)\\n  * <::marker>ML-Bench: [ ` evaluation/ml_bench ` ](/root/openhands/-/tree/main/evaluation/ml_bench)\\n  * <::marker>APIBench: [ ` evaluation/gorilla ` ](/root/openhands/-/tree/main/evaluation/gorilla)\\n  * <::marker>ToolQA: [ ` evaluation/toolqa ` ](/root/openhands/-/tree/main/evaluation/toolqa)\\n  * <::marker>AiderBench: [ ` evaluation/aider_bench ` ](/root/openhands/-/tree/main/evaluation/aider_bench)\\n\\n\\n\\n###  <::after> Web Browsing \\n\\n  * <::marker>WebArena: [ ` evaluation/webarena ` ](/root/openhands/-/tree/main/evaluation/webarena)\\n  * <::marker>MiniWob++: [ ` evaluation/miniwob ` ](/root/openhands/-/tree/main/evaluation/miniwob)\\n\\n\\n\\n###  <::after> Misc. Assistance \\n\\n  * <::marker>GAIA: [ ` evaluation/gaia ` ](/root/openhands/-/tree/main/evaluation/gaia)\\n  * <::marker>GPQA: [ ` evaluation/gpqa ` ](/root/openhands/-/tree/main/evaluation/gpqa)\\n  * <::marker>AgentBench: [ ` evaluation/agent_bench ` ](/root/openhands/-/tree/main/evaluation/agent_bench)\\n  * <::marker>MINT: [ ` evaluation/mint ` ](/root/openhands/-/tree/main/evaluation/mint)\\n  * <::marker>Entity deduction Arena (EDA): [ ` evaluation/EDA ` ](/root/openhands/-/tree/main/evaluation/EDA)\\n  * <::marker>ProofWriter: [ ` evaluation/logic_reasoning ` ](/root/openhands/-/tree/main/evaluation/logic_reasoning)\\n\\n\\n\\n##  <::after> Before everything begins: Setup Environment and LLM Configuration \\n\\nPlease follow instruction [ here ](https://github.com/All-Hands-AI/OpenHands/blob/main/Development.md) to setup your local development environment and LLM. \\n\\nOpenHands in development mode uses ` config.toml ` to keep track of most configurations. \\n\\nHere\\'s an example configuration file you can use to define and use multiple LLMs: \\n    \\n    \\n    [llm]\\n    # IMPORTANT: add your API key here, and set the model to the one you want to evaluate\\n    model = \"gpt-4o-2024-05-13\"\\n    api_key = \"sk-XXX\"\\n    \\n    [llm.eval_gpt4_1106_preview_llm]\\n    model = \"gpt-4-1106-preview\"\\n    api_key = \"XXX\"\\n    temperature = 0.0\\n    \\n    [llm.eval_some_openai_compatible_model_llm]\\n    model = \"openai/MODEL_NAME\"\\n    base_url = \"https://OPENAI_COMPATIBLE_URL/v1\"\\n    api_key = \"XXX\"\\n    temperature = 0.0\\n\\n###  <::after> Result Visualization \\n\\nCheck [ this huggingface space ](https://huggingface.co/spaces/OpenHands/evaluation) for visualization of existing experimental results. \\n\\n###  <::after> Upload your results \\n\\nYou can start your own fork of [ our huggingface evaluation outputs ](https://huggingface.co/spaces/OpenHands/evaluation) and submit a PR of your evaluation results to our hosted huggingface repo via PR following the guide [ here ](https://huggingface.co/docs/hub/en/repositories-pull-requests-discussions#pull-requests-and-discussions) . \\n', url='http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/openhands/-/tree/main/evaluation', trigger_by_action='browse_interactive', screenshot_path='/outputs/.browser_screenshots/screenshot_20251108_045506_733118.png', error=False, observation=<ObservationType.BROWSE: 'browse'>, goal_image_urls=[], open_pages_urls=['http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/openhands/-/tree/main/evaluation'], active_page_index=0, last_browser_action=\"\\n\\n# Let's explore the evaluation directory structure more thoroughly to understand all benchmarks\\ngoto('http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/openhands/-/tree/main/evaluation')\\nnoop(2000)\\n\\n\", last_browser_action_error='', focused_element_bid='81'), MessageAction(content='<|STEP_COMPLETED|>\\n\\nI have successfully analyzed the repository structure and identified all available benchmarks. From the evaluation directory, I can see there are 16 benchmark directories organized into 3 main categories:\\n\\n**Software Engineering (8 benchmarks):**\\n- SWE-Bench\\n- HumanEvalFix\\n- BIRD\\n- BioCoder\\n- ML-Bench\\n- APIBench (Gorilla)\\n- ToolQA\\n- AiderBench\\n\\n**Web Browsing (2 benchmarks):**\\n- WebArena\\n- MiniWob++\\n\\n**Miscellaneous Assistance (6 benchmarks):**\\n- GAIA\\n- GPQA\\n- AgentBench\\n- MINT\\n- Entity Deduction Arena (EDA)\\n- ProofWriter (Logic Reasoning)\\n\\nThis comprehensive analysis provides the foundation for categorizing the benchmarks into task domains for the presentation.', image_urls=None, wait_for_response=True, action=<ActionType.MESSAGE: 'message'>, security_risk=None), MessageAction(content='Please continue working on the task on whatever approach you think is suitable.\\nIf you think you have solved the task, please finish the interaction.\\nIMPORTANT: YOU SHOULD NEVER ASK FOR HUMAN HELP.\\nIf you want to give up, run: <execute_bash> exit </execute_bash>.\\n', image_urls=None, wait_for_response=False, action=<ActionType.MESSAGE: 'message'>, security_risk=None), RecallAction(recall_type='knowledge', query='Please continue working on the task on whatever approach you think is suitable.\\nIf you think you have solved the task, please finish the interaction.\\nIMPORTANT: YOU SHOULD NEVER ASK FOR HUMAN HELP.\\nIf you want to give up, run: <execute_bash> exit </execute_bash>.\\n', thought='', action=<ActionType.RECALL: 'recall'>), MessageAction(content='Continuing with next planned step..2:Categorize the identified benchmarks into distinct task domains based on their functionality and goals', image_urls=None, wait_for_response=False, action=<ActionType.MESSAGE: 'message'>, security_risk=None), MessageAction(content='You are currently executing a planned step. Follow these instructions EXACTLY:\\n\\nTASK: Categorize the identified benchmarks into distinct task domains based on their functionality and goals \\n\\nCurrent Progress: 3 step / 7 steps\\n\\nGuidelines:  \\n\\nRULES:\\n- Do NOT deviate from this step.\\n- Use available tools to make PROGRESS.\\n- When you have FULLY and SUCCESSFULLY completed this step, output ONLY the following line and nothing else:\\n  <|STEP_COMPLETED|>\\n\\n', image_urls=None, wait_for_response=False, action=<ActionType.MESSAGE: 'message'>, security_risk=None), MessageAction(content='Based on my analysis of the OpenHands repository structure and the README documentation, I have successfully categorized the 16 benchmarks into distinct task domains based on their functionality and goals:\\n\\n**Software Engineering Domain (8 benchmarks):**\\n- SWE-Bench: Real-world software engineering tasks from GitHub issues\\n- HumanEvalFix: Code repair and bug fixing tasks\\n- BIRD: Database-oriented programming tasks\\n- BioCoder: Bioinformatics and computational biology tasks\\n- ML-Bench: Machine learning pipeline development\\n- APIBench (Gorilla): API calling and integration tasks\\n- ToolQA: Tool usage and API integration\\n- AiderBench: Code generation and modification tasks\\n\\n**Web Browsing & Interaction Domain (2 benchmarks):**\\n- WebArena: Realistic web interaction and navigation tasks\\n- MiniWob++: Web automation and interaction tasks\\n\\n**General Assistance & Reasoning Domain (6 benchmarks):**\\n- GAIA: General AI assistance and reasoning tasks\\n- GPQA: Graduate-level reasoning and problem solving\\n- AgentBench: Multi-domain agent performance evaluation\\n- MINT: Mathematical reasoning and problem solving\\n- EDA (Entity Deduction Arena): Logical reasoning and deduction\\n- ProofWriter (Logic Reasoning): Formal reasoning and proof generation\\n\\nThese categories accurately reflect the different capabilities of OpenHands agents across software development, web interaction, and general AI assistance domains.\\n\\n<|STEP_COMPLETED|>', image_urls=None, wait_for_response=True, action=<ActionType.MESSAGE: 'message'>, security_risk=None), MessageAction(content='Please continue working on the task on whatever approach you think is suitable.\\nIf you think you have solved the task, please finish the interaction.\\nIMPORTANT: YOU SHOULD NEVER ASK FOR HUMAN HELP.\\nIf you want to give up, run: <execute_bash> exit </execute_bash>.\\n', image_urls=None, wait_for_response=False, action=<ActionType.MESSAGE: 'message'>, security_risk=None), RecallAction(recall_type='knowledge', query='Please continue working on the task on whatever approach you think is suitable.\\nIf you think you have solved the task, please finish the interaction.\\nIMPORTANT: YOU SHOULD NEVER ASK FOR HUMAN HELP.\\nIf you want to give up, run: <execute_bash> exit </execute_bash>.\\n', thought='', action=<ActionType.RECALL: 'recall'>), MessageAction(content='Continuing with next planned step.